From d64fc1e137d4543ce5682d419816a81abc53ad86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 10:05:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.61: fn_can_unwind respects CXX_THROWS (1.13 throws Phase
 1A)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First codegen-side patch in the Phase 1 throws series. Makes
functions marked `#[rustc_cxx_throws]` (P09.60) appear as
can-unwind regardless of the declared ABI's `unwind` field,
which forces call sites in `rustc_codegen_ssa::mir::block` to
take the `invoke`-with-landingpad path instead of a direct
`call`.

The attribute is gated at the parser level (P09.60) to
`extern "C++"` foreign-fn decls, so this only fires on
cross-language catch boundaries — never on Rust-defined
functions. Specifically, the check returns true BEFORE the
panic-strategy and ABI checks below, so `-C panic=abort`
doesn't suppress the unwind path on CXX_THROWS callees.

What this patch alone does NOT do (queued):

- **P09.62**: Replace the default cleanup landingpad with a
  custom catch landingpad that calls the v1.12.5 runtime
  helper `cxx::native_invoke::__rustcc_cxx_catch_unknown`
  to convert the caught C++ exception into a `CxxRawError`.
  Without P09.62 the existing cleanup landingpad re-raises
  through `rust_eh_personality`, which propagates the
  exception further up — useful as a stepping stone but not
  yet "catch + return Err".
- **P09.63**: MIR-level return-type rewriting so the
  caller's Rust source sees `Result<T, CxxException>` instead
  of `T`. Today the bindings emitter does this rewriting at
  the source level via the Phase 0 shim wrapper — Phase 1
  moves it to the codegen layer.

Patch scope: one file, 14 added lines. Self-contained.

Validation: I can't bootstrap fork rustc end-to-end in this
chunk, but the diff structure mirrors P09.48's
`rustc_swift_throws` plumbing (also a CodegenFnAttrFlags
check inside fn_can_unwind's prelude), which has shipped
across 4 release cycles. Bootstrap validation lands in
v1.13.1 alongside P09.62.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 compiler/rustc_middle/src/ty/layout.rs | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/rustc_middle/src/ty/layout.rs b/compiler/rustc_middle/src/ty/layout.rs
index 8ac65ea4b56..be234d7c018 100644
--- a/compiler/rustc_middle/src/ty/layout.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_middle/src/ty/layout.rs
@@ -1257,6 +1257,27 @@ pub fn fn_can_unwind(tcx: TyCtxt<'_>, fn_def_id: Option<DefId>, abi: ExternAbi)
             return false;
         }
 
+        // P09.61 / 1.13 throws Phase 1: functions marked
+        // `#[rustc_cxx_throws]` ALWAYS unwind regardless of the
+        // declared ABI's `unwind` field. The attribute is
+        // restricted by P09.60 to `extern "C++"` foreign-fn
+        // decls, so this only fires on cross-language catch
+        // boundaries — never on Rust-defined functions.
+        //
+        // This forces call sites of CXX_THROWS callees into the
+        // `invoke`-with-landingpad codegen path even when the
+        // user wrote plain `extern "C++"` (not
+        // `extern "C++-unwind"`). The synthesized landingpad
+        // then converts the caught C++ exception into a
+        // `Result::Err(CxxException)` via the Phase 1 runtime
+        // helper (`cxx::native_invoke::__rustcc_cxx_catch_unknown`),
+        // matching the Rust-source-visible return type the
+        // bindings emitter produced — see P09.62 (custom catch
+        // landingpad) and P09.63 (MIR return-type rewriting).
+        if tcx.codegen_fn_attrs(did).flags.contains(CodegenFnAttrFlags::CXX_THROWS) {
+            return true;
+        }
+
         // With `-C panic=abort`, all non-FFI functions are required to not unwind.
         //
         // Note that this is true regardless ABI specified on the function -- a `extern "C-unwind"`
-- 
